  "why": "The paper proposes CAGFuzz to generate transferable adversarial examples for discovering errors in standard DNN models and for improving model accuracy through retraining. The method's evaluation focuses on its ability to find errors in undefended models (RQ2) and to enhance model robustness by using the generated examples for adversarial training (RQ3). The paper demonstrates how to *build* a safeguard (a more robust, retrained model), but it does not design its fuzzer to target or test an already-defended model, nor does it demonstrate a successful bypass of such a safeguard. The experimental setup tests against original, undefended models and then shows the positive effect of retraining with the adversarial examples, rather than attempting to find inputs that fool the newly hardened model.",
